Article 2 (Scope of Accredited Research Institutes, Including Universities)
The term "accredited research institutes, including universities" in Article 19 (4) 5 of the Constitutional Court Act means any of the following:
1. A university-affiliated research institute whose primary subject of research is law, established by a university, industrial university, university of education, junior college, open university, or technical college that has been established pursuant to Article 4 (1) of the Higher Education Act or established with authorization from the Minister of Education pursuant to paragraph (2) of the same Article;
2. A government-funded research institute established under Article 8 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes;
3. A research institute funded by a local government and established under Article 4 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Local Government-Funded Research Institutes;
4. A research institute eligible for protection and fostering by the Government under the Specific Research Institutes Support Act.
